  "source": "// The annotation layer, end to end (docs/prompts/35): named phrases over the\n// notes, form markers at measure:beat positions, and a harmony lane.\n//\n// Nothing here is interpreted. The chord symbols are recorded and printed;\n// musa never derives notes from them, never checks the notes under them, and\n// has no opinion about the voice leading between them. Sections and phrases\n// name the structure a reader already hears; they change no sounding note.\npiece \"Annotated\" {\n    tempo 1/4 = 96;\n    meter 4/4;\n    key a minor;\n\n    score {\n        section \"Exposition\" at 1:1;\n        section \"Development\" at 3:1;\n\n        harmony {\n            at 1:1 am;\n            at 2:1 fmaj7;\n            at 3:1 e7;\n            at 4:1 am;\n        }\n\n        part piano {\n            clef treble;\n\n            voice lead {\n                phrase \"antecedent\" {\n                    a4 1/4;\n                    c5 1/4;\n                    e5 1/2;\n                    f5 1/2;\n                    e5 1/2;\n                }\n                phrase \"consequent\" {\n                    b4 1/4;\n                    e5 1/4;\n                    g#5 1/2;\n                    a5 1;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
